entry.content:
check_tx: description, inputSchema  +a message to sign (message: {kind: personal_sign | eth_sign, data, origin?}), -(typedData: Permit, Permit2, TransferWithAuthorization) +(typedData), an ERC-4337 user operation (userOp, with entryPoint), a type-4 authorizationList (alone or with the transaction), the wallet request as the agent would send it (rpc: {method, params} for personal_sign, eth_sign, eth_signTypedData_v4 or eth_sendTransaction), +The coin bought's name and symbol are scanned for instructions aimed at AI agents. +never ALLOW: -never ALLOW; a +high when it sends ETH, and BLOCK at 0.05 ETH or more, or any ETH to an addre  parameters: +input.authorizationList input.authorizationList description: A type-4 (EIP-7702) transaction's authorizationList, or a signAuthorization alone (no to, no data): [{chainId, address, nonce, yParity, r, s}]. A delegate Toll has verified by code hash is WARN; any other is BLOCK input.authorization_list input.authorization_list description: The same list under its snake_case name +input.entryPoint input.entryPoint description: The userOp's EntryPoint address (0x + 40 hex); an EntryPoint Toll does not know is a warning +input.intent input.intent description: Optional: what the agent means to do, co
presign_risk_report: description, inputSchema  -typedData?}, +typedData?, authorizationList?},  parameters: -typedData?} +typedData?, authorizationList? (EIP-7702: bound into the subject digest, listed as a coverage gap, not applied)}
watch_coin: description  +(with more watched coins it takes longer)
